In GsPermissions.kt, make `takeGsRoute()` reject anything outside the allowlist, the same way `isSidebarRoute` works:

```kotlin
private fun Intent.takeGsRoute(): String? =
    runCatching { getStringExtra(EXTRA_GS_ROUTE) }.getOrNull()
        ?.also { removeExtra(EXTRA_GS_ROUTE) }
        ?.takeIf { it.isGsRoute() }
```

`isGsRoute()` should accept only the routes the app itself sends: GS_ROUTE_PERMISSION, Home, Settings, VaultLock, and the album routes that `gsAlbumRoute` / `Screen.AlbumDetail.createRoute("filter:...")` produce. Match the album routes on their exact prefix, plus Favorites, Moments or CollageMaker if `gsAlbumRoute` returns them.

As a backstop against a crash, wrap the `navigate` call at :201 in `runCatching`.
